  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Exponential Family - Bernoulli</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The probability mass function for the Bernoulli distribution is given by:</p>
<p>\[ f(y; {@p_var@}) = {@p_var@}^y (1 - {@p_var@})^{1-y} \]</p>
<p>Show that this belongs to the exponential family of distributions by rewriting it in the form:</p>
<p>\[ f(y; \theta) = a(\theta)b(y) \exp(yQ(\theta)) \]</p>
<p>Identify the following components in terms of \({@p_var@}\):</p>
<p>\(Q({@p_var@}) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>\(a({@p_var@}) = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>\(b(y) = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Rewrite the density function:</p>
<p>\[ f(y; {@p_var@}) = {@p_var@}^y (1 - {@p_var@})^{1-y} \]</p>
<p>\[ = (1 - {@p_var@}) \left( \frac{{@p_var@}}{1 - {@p_var@}} \right)^y \]</p>
<p>\[ = (1 - {@p_var@}) \exp \left( y \log \left( \frac{{@p_var@}}{1 - {@p_var@}} \right) \right) \]</p>
<p>Comparing this to \( f(y; \theta) = a(\theta)b(y) \exp(yQ(\theta)) \):</p>
<p>\[ Q({@p_var@}) = \log \left( \frac{{@p_var@}}{1 - {@p_var@}} \right) \]</p>
<p>\[ a({@p_var@}) = 1 - {@p_var@} \]</p>
<p>\[ b(y) = 1 \]</p>
<p>The natural parameter is \(Q({@p_var@})\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
